1
00:06:42,352 --> 00:06:48,352
Welcome to the Theatre of the Absurd.

2
00:13:24,705 --> 00:13:30,705
The Theatre Bizarre is a horror film directed by Tom Savini.

3
00:20:07,058 --> 00:20:13,058
Down a seedy city street in her neighborhood, young Enola Penny is
obsessed with what appears to be a long abandoned theatre.

4
00:26:49,411 --> 00:26:55,411
One night, she sees that the front door is slightly ajar
and impulsively decides to sneak inside.

5
00:33:31,764 --> 00:33:37,764
But there in the dark, decrepit auditorium, a show
unlike any other unfolds before her eyes.

6
00:40:14,117 --> 00:40:20,117
Its host is an eerie human puppet named Peg Poett who will introduce Penny to six tales of the bizarre: A couple traveling in a remote part of the French Pyrenees cross paths with a lustful witch; A paranoid lover faces the wrath of a partner who has been pushed to her limit; The Freudian dreams of an unfaithful husband
blur the lines between fantasy and reality; The horrors of the real world are interpreted through the mind of a child; A woman addicted to other people's memories gets her fix through the vitreous fluid of her victims' eyeballs; And a perverse obsession with sweets turns sour for a couple in too deep.

7
00:46:56,470 --> 00:47:02,470
Peg Poett, played by Udo Kier.

8
00:53:38,823 --> 00:53:44,823
Enola Penny, played by Virginia Newcomb.

9
01:00:21,176 --> 01:00:27,176
Squalid Woman, played by Amanda Marquardt.

10
01:07:03,529 --> 01:07:09,529
Gypsy, played by Amelia M. Gotham.

11
01:13:45,882 --> 01:13:51,882
Mere Antoinette, played by Catriona MacColl.

12
01:20:28,235 --> 01:20:34,235
Martin, played by Shane Woodward.

13
01:27:10,588 --> 01:27:16,588
The Theatre Bizarre is a 2011 American horror anthology film.

14
01:33:52,941 --> 01:33:58,941
The six segments are directed by Douglas Buck, Buddy Giovinazzo, David
Gregory, Karim Hussain, Tom Savini and Richard Stanley.

15
01:40:35,294 --> 01:40:41,294
The wraparound segments featuring Udo Kier were directed by Jeremy Kasten.

16
01:47:17,647 --> 01:47:23,647
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
